@title How a return gets decided
@subtitle Greenmoor Apparel customer care, guide for agents
@date 2026-10-12

## Decision flow

diagram flow dir=TB title="Return request decision flow"
flow: req "Return requested" user
flow: window "Within 30 days of delivery?" decision
flow: final "Final-sale item?" decision
flow: decline "Decline return" svc
flow: label "Issue prepaid label" svc
flow: recv "Item received at warehouse" store
flow: insp "Inspection passes?" decision focus
flow: credit "Offer store credit at 50 percent" svc
flow: value "Order value over 200 dollars?" decision
flow: lead "Returns Lead review" team focus
flow: refund "Refund to original payment" svc
flow: req -> window
flow: window -> decline : no
flow: window -> final : yes
flow: final -> decline : yes
flow: final -> label : no
flow: label -> recv -> insp
flow: insp -> credit : no
flow: insp -> value : yes
flow: value -> lead : yes
flow: value -> refund : no
flow: lead -> refund : approved

## Service levels

table = step,target; Prepaid label issued,Within 1 business hour of request; Inspection,Within 2 business days of arrival; Refund posted,Within 3 business days of inspection; Returns Lead review,Within 1 business day

## Exceptions

- **Damaged on arrival:** skip the 30-day and final-sale checks.
- **Gift returns:** always get store credit.
- **More than 4 returns in 90 days:** route the customer to the Returns Lead.
